<http://data.silknow.org/object/ac741613-4ecd-3929-a71d-f0177c36a9d1>
        a                       ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment            "Brocaded, with floral pattern; Iran; 1700s."@en , "Brocade woven in silk and silver-gilt thread  on a ground of double texture (tabby weave). The fabric consists of two pieces of silk cloth, interwoven only where the pattern appears. The pattern depicts two symmetrical flowering plants, in gold and light green on a white ground. The piece of cloth forming the backing is brownish yellow."@en ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note        "Brocaded, with floral pattern; Iran; 1700s."@en , "Brocade woven in silk and silver-gilt thread  on a ground of double texture (tabby weave). The fabric consists of two pieces of silk cloth, interwoven only where the pattern appears. The pattern depicts two symmetrical flowering plants, in gold and light green on a white ground. The piece of cloth forming the backing is brownish yellow."@en ;
